      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T18:42:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`concurrent gets and puts safe.` Agreed that the actual map is thread safe.  The issue is that the state machine may be invalidated while a copy is held.\n\nIf the client state machine provides the equivalent of a reference, with reference counts, then no locks are required.  But if the state machine is deleted by another thread without references then this would break.\n\nI\u0027m don\u0027t understand all the nuances java\u0027s `ConcurrentHashMap\u003c\u003e`",
      "parentUuid": "8a2c727b_3b3afccf",
      "range": {
